{
  "summary": "Subclasses Python's `http.client.HTTPConnection` in the functional test framework to apply `set_ephemeral_port_range()` on newly created client sockets before connecting. Replaces direct `http.client.HTTPConnection` instantiations in the RPC auth proxy and several functional tests with this wrapper to avoid ephemeral port overlap on BSD systems.",
  "problem": "On FreeBSD and OpenBSD, the default ephemeral port ranges overlap with the functional test suite's reserved port range. Because Python's standard `http.client` manages its own socket creation internally, it bypasses the test framework's `set_ephemeral_port_range()` socket option, allowing outgoing HTTP/RPC connections directed to closed ports to select identical local ports and connect to themselves.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author encountered this while stress-testing FreeBSD CI in #36147: \"the wrong-RPC-port startup check failed with BadStatusLine: POST / HTTP/1.1 because the client read back its own request.\""
  ],
