  "card": "Subclasses Python's HTTPConnection in the functional test framework to configure ephemeral port ranges before establishing connections. On FreeBSD and OpenBSD, default ephemeral port ranges overlap with test ports, causing http.client sockets to occasionally assign identical source and destination ports and connect to themselves when targeting closed ports. The author encountered this while stress-testing native FreeBSD CI in #36147, where a wrong-RPC-port startup check failed with BadStatusLine after reading its own request. This change stabilizes functional test runs on BSD platforms and unblocks native FreeBSD CI in #36147.",
